WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:06.464
Cities have a phenomenon called
the urban heat Island effect,

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:09.759
which is primarily due
to the generation of heat

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:13.388
by cars, air
conditioning, buildings, people.

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:17.308
We know that people in cities
are disproportionately affected

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:18.685
by climate change.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:22.272 line:83%
So I was curious to see how
we can use cities as part of

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.525 line:83%
the solutions to both mitigate
and adapt to climate change.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.320
I had read an article
about how new paint

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.282
was being developed that could
absorb some heat

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:35.243
and reduce temperatures
of surfaces.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:38.288
And I know that endless graphics

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:42.083
and tables
don't really move people.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:48.506
I heard about our new dean
of the Art School, Kym Pinder,

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.926
who is an expert in urban art.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.554
I reached out to her
and I said, “hey,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:58.224
is there something that we could
do together to move people

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.478
and inform them, inspire them
through art in cities?”

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:04.814 line:83%
We decided, wow,
we should try and build

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:08.359 line:83%
some kind of relationship,
some programing together

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:12.447
around community, mural making
and this cooling paint.

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:16.951
You know, we have a mural
that is on Mill Street

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.745
in New Haven.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.331
That was the final result.

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:22.957
But I should say it's not over.

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:27.170
We're going to build this
project also around training up

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.089
local artists
in the art of mural making.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:35.637
And so, then to actually create
a sustainable art community

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.640
for so many of the empty walls
that are in New Haven.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.060
Art can pull you into thinking
about an issue that you

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.355
may not have wanted to,
or even thought you ever would.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:48.066
And I think that's
the storytelling capability

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:49.275
of all the arts.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:53.321
If art or cool murals can
inspire people

00:01:53.321 --> 00:01:56.866
to have conversations and then
ultimately act on climate change

00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:59.369
it's a success.

